# XML, TEI, and Digital Libraries in the Humanities.

**Authors:** Nellhaus, Tobin

## Abstract
Describes the history and major features of XML and TEI, discusses their potential utility for the creation of digital libraries, and focuses on XML's application in the humanities, particularly theater and drama studies. Highlights include HTML and hyperlinks; the impact of XML on text encoding and document access; and XML and academic librarianship. (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ647515

